    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d909">

                <pb facs="0938" n="926" sameAs="frus:frus1941v02/pg926"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">711.52/200: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in Spain</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Weddell</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Madrid</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1941-10-01T19:00:00+01:00">October 1, 1941—7
                            p.m.</date>
                        <lb/> [Received 9:04 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>873. My 868, September 30, 7 p.m. If the Department approves I intend at my
                    approaching interview with General Franco to talk with him concerning economic
                    cooperation along the lines set forth in my following telegram No. 874<anchor
                        n="41" xml:id="d909-f1"/> and to leave a memorandum with him to that
                    effect.</p>
                <p>Following this I propose to inform him verbally that in my interview with the
                    Foreign Minister on Tuesday when the question of gasoline supplies from the
                    United States was mentioned he had remarked that if Spain’s non-belligerency
                    meant anything to the British cause Spain must not be “strangled” in respect to
                    motor fuel. And that further in this connection I wished to suggest to him in
                    the most friendly way that a threat of belligerency on the part of his
                    Government would automatically render it impossible for the United States to
                    continue to discuss economic cooperation.</p>
                <p>As I may see the Caudillo on Friday<anchor n="42" xml:id="d909-f2"/> but probably
                    on Saturday the Department’s early reply is requested.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Weddell</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
